{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N2"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 136, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Turning an empty 0->3 edge into a residual shortcut adds a gradient path without removing any computation."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on the direct path with a skip removes learnable capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "In parameter-poor skip-heavy cells, another identity path further starves the network of computation."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-dominated cells, an extra skip does not compensate for missing convolutions and hurts accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a 0->3 shortcut, the new 1->3 skip supplies the cell's only residual path, so it matters more."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing an existing convolution on edge 4 sacrifices capacity, unlike replacing none or pooling."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In pooling-heavy cells, swapping out the sole conv on edge 4 for a skip removes most of the learnable computation."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv to a cell with no convolutions yields a large capacity gain."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Skip-dominated cells lack learnable ops, so a new 3x3 conv brings